    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1470">

                <pb facs="0762" n="2464" xml:id="pg2464"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">641.86A/3–1152: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1470<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of
                            State to the Embassy in Saudi
                        Arabia</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d1470-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-03-24T12:34:00-05:00">March 24, 1952—12:34
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>351. You may inform Feisal US is moved by
                    earnestness of his and HM’s attitude this problem
                        (Embtels 474 and 477, Mar 10 and
                        11<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1470-f2"/>) and intends making serious approach to
                    UK (Deptel 4691 to London Mar 24, rptd Jidda
                        350<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1470-f3"/>). Approach made out of sincere concern
                    for relations between our two good friends despite delicacy always attendant
                    when outsider becomes involved family quarrel. Must similarly enjoin SAG, however, to meet any Brit approach halfway.
                    Compromise cannot be one-sided. Inflexible view . . . re . . . rights to land
                    and people not conducive success . . . . This alone cld block progress.<anchor
                        n="4" xml:id="d1470-f4"/></p>
                <p>You might also assure Feisal we know of
                    no Brit plan unite Iraq, Kuwait (Embtel 474),
                    and feel sure there is none. If this suggested to SAG by recent visit Sheikh Kuwait to Iraq you might add we know
                    this visit caught Brit by surprise and was initiated by IG. Wld also appear illegal for Brit support absorption Kuwait by
                    Iraq and lose preferential position UK enjoys in Kuwait. Dept notes SA tendency be over-suspicious Brit which is
                    destructive mutual confidence so necessary for conducting negots under best
                    auspices.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"><hi
                                    rendition="#small-caps"
                    >Acheson</hi></hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1470-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1470-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated as telegram 4692 to London and 593 to Baghdad. Drafted by Awalt and cleared by EUR, BNA, and NEA.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1470-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1470-f2-content">
                <p><ref target="#d1467">Documents 1467</ref> and <ref target="#d1468"
                    >1468</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1470-f3" n="3" xml:id="d1470-f3-content">
                <p><ref target="#d1469"><hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi></ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1470-f4" n="4" xml:id="d1470-f4-content">
                <p>Telegram 551 from Jidda, Apr. 8, reported the message in this telegram had been
                    delivered to Faisal the previous
                    evening. (641.86A/4–852)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
